The web app used to load these two from fonts.googleapis.com at runtime instead.
That sent every page load to a third party, in a product whose landing page sells
"nothing leaves your device" — so it now self-hosts them, and the licenses moved
in here with the binaries. Because the bundler emits the .woff2 files as opaque
hashed assets with no license of their own, the two .txt files live in
ui/public/fonts/ and are copied verbatim into dist/fonts/ alongside them.

The OFL is permissive and imposes no conditions on the surrounding Apache-2.0
