`ui/vendor/zipp-wasm/` holds a prebuilt WebAssembly build of the Zipp JavaScript
engine. OAIY uses it to execute untrusted package workflows in an engine with no
host capabilities — see ui/vendor/oaiy-core/src/zipp-executor.ts.

It ships as committed bytes rather than a build step because ui/ is a standalone
Vite app: `npm install && npm run dev` must work without a Rust toolchain and
without a sibling checkout. The build provenance, the source commit, and the
SHA-256 of the exact module are recorded in ui/vendor/zipp-wasm/README.md; the
SHA is asserted by ui/tests/zipp-executor.mjs so a refresh cannot quietly
substitute a different engine.

Zipp is Apache-2.0, the same license as OAIY, so it imposes no conditions beyond
this attribution and the retained license text.
